<p>Mobile and portable trackers are the most common way people first get on the APRS network. Because they're constantly changing position — and often changing which digipeaters they can hear — path settings matter more here than almost anywhere else.</p>

<p>See also <a href="/home-station-settings/" class="text-signal-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-500">Home Station Settings</a> if you're configuring a fixed station instead.</p>
